  "findings": [
    "Every arm passes the complete section-6.1 screen with two to three orders of magnitude of margin: mean KL 1.0e-5 to 3.5e-5 (limit 1e-3), p95 6.6e-5 to 2.5e-4 (limit 5e-3), p99 8.3e-5 to 4.4e-4 (limit 2e-2), max 1.1e-4 to 7.0e-4 (limit 5e-2), and top-1 100% overall and in every category.",
    "Repeats are bit-identical in all four arms, so the gate is deterministic at both the native-graph and eager paths.",
    "The UD-Q4_K_S generated-ID near-ties recorded in the paired production artifact are not a verification-arithmetic failure: at identical contexts the K_S verifier reproduces the AR logits to max KL 1.07e-4 with 100% top-1. They are free-running near-tie drift under the section-4.1 production profile.",
    "gfx1100 declares GGUF_SPECDEC2_NATIVE_TARGET_GRAPH_MAX_CONTEXT = 95, so the captured native target graph only runs while root_position + rows <= 95. At a 512-token root the production caller takes the eager multi-row verifier (fallback_reason=\"target_graph_context_bucket_miss\"), which the 512-token arms measure directly. Both paths pass.",
    "The residual KL is the AR route's rows==1 local32 IQ decode owner against the verifier's strict per-row GEMV; the largest logit difference is 0.15-0.17 absolute on a wide-margin distribution. Phase 4 replaces the verifier owner with the same local32 family, so this residual is the quantity Phase 4 should drive toward zero."
  ],
  "coverage_gaps": [
    "c2/c4/c8 widths and batch-composition invariance need a multi-request caller; this gate is c1.",
    "Contexts above 512 (4096, 32768) are not measured. Beyond the gfx1100 native bucket they use the same eager multi-row verifier measured here, but the split-K attention schedule differs.",
    "Q8 alpha/beta recurrent transitions are not isolated as their own scope.",
    "Sampling is out of scope; the serving path is greedy here."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Correctness only: no rate is claimed and none may be derived from this artifact.",
    "The gate compares two production routes against each other, not production against the strict quant route. That comparison is the combined-stack gate in scripts/gguf_ud_combined_stack_gate.py."
  ]
}
